[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m, inside the empty [38;5;153m<main>[39m:

  [90m<[34mlabel[90m>[39m
    [90m<[34minput[90m [36mtype[90m=[31m"checkbox"[90m [36mname[90m=[31m"done"[90m>[39m
    Example task
  [90m</[34mlabel[90m>[39m

  It's a plain HTML checkbox, so the browser handles the on/off state with no JavaScript. Wrapping it in the [38;5;153m<label>[39m
  means clicking the text also toggles it, and screen readers announce the text with the checkbox.

  The state isn't saved, so it resets when the page reloads. Change "Example task" to your real item text, and copy the
  [38;5;153m<label>[39m block for each extra item. I haven't committed the change.

  If you want more later, I can add saving with [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m, strike through finished items, or build the list with
  JavaScript.

